<p>As a rising power, India is a critical actor in the Indo-Pacific and an increasingly consequential power in international affairs. India is also an important political and strategic partner for Australia. This course will enable students to develop a strong understanding of the politics and foreign policy of India. It will examine key ideas that inform India’s foreign policy and its strategic culture and study political institutions that inform and shape foreign policy. It will explore India’s major bilateral, regional and international strategic engagements, including its strategy within the broader Indo-Pacific in the contemporary period.</p>



